gned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-3,3) & ={f}_{y}(-3,3)(y-(3)) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(6)(y-(3)) \\\\ z-(-1) & =6 y - 18 \\\\ z & =6 y - 19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-3,3,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{x=-3 \\\\ z=6 y - 19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-3,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=6 y - 19$ (or $6 y - z - 19=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,6,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,6,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j + 6 k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,1,6⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["7a486d1b-902f-5597-a6ae-36fd96e6212e"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "1517b8a7-b8eb-5039-9dec-9ce81c5652e6" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124439.py"} [:db/add 17592186124439 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186124439 :knowledge-point/questions ["48d0933d-38f4-5fca-ac17-2cb0bd7b696b" "76fc75e5-bc34-5a11-827a-718027bfa6d6" "24dbd77f-2590-58ef-821c-6bd1e8a62bdc" "e5e09c79-be5e-59c8-bad2-508a4b285ff7" "87773f30-7347-58c3-bc15-641532470ff8" "322047e2-3976-5636-bcd1-e92ee6b570c4" "8f308815-8a1f-5bcf-b629-6357db90aa05" "dd9d8206-b563-5e86-ab9a-f167bb3c1e2b" "055263bb-00e6-5ecd-9052-3f0991382dda" "f350a280-28d9-5c60-b2e4-617d820b96d3"]} [:db/ensure 17592186124439 :knowledge-point/validate]]
